  "question": {
    "text": "A random variable <math><mi>X</mi></math>&nbsp;follows binomial probability distribution with probability&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp; with mean as&nbsp;<math><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo></math> probability of success as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi></math>&nbsp;and probability of failure as&nbsp;<math><mi>q</mi></math> such that <math><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo></math> If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#931;</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>28</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;then the probability of exactly <math><mn>2</mn></math> success is",
